//==
// # Model mesh topology: types
//
// The combinatorial structure of a model mesh, read from its elements alone: the 1-skeleton with
// its incidence (MeshEdgeTable), the connected components (MeshComponents), and per component the
// counts from which closedness, orientation, the Euler characteristic, and the genus follow.
//
// Orientation is a 2-colouring of half-edges: every element side is an undirected edge traversed
// one way or the other, coloured +1 when it runs from the lower vertex index to the higher and -1
// otherwise. The mesh is coherently oriented at an edge with two sides exactly when the two colours
// differ, which is when the edge's DirectionSum is 0.
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - The edge table
//  - Components

//==
// # The edge table

// The 1-skeleton of a ModelMesh with its incidence: every undirected edge that some element side
// lies on, once. Edges is canonical and sorted, as the stdlib's UndirectedEdgeList states (each
// pair A < B, pairs in lexicographic order), so an edge's position is its UndirectedEdgeIndex.
// ElementCounts[k] is the number of element sides on edge k, which is the number of elements
// incident to it when no element repeats a vertex. DirectionSums[k] adds +1 for each side running
// from Edges[k].A to Edges[k].B and -1 for each side running back: the orientation parity. A side
// whose two ends are one vertex (an element that repeats a vertex) is not an edge of the complex
// and is not listed; HasRepeatedCorner reports it. The stdlib's UndirectedEdgeAdjacency is not used
// because it stores at most two faces per edge and so cannot hold the non-manifold edges this table
// exists to find.
type MeshEdgeTable
    implements IValue
{
    Edges: UndirectedEdgeList;
    ElementCounts: Array<Integer>;
    DirectionSums: Array<Integer>;
}

//==
// # Components

// A zero-based index of a connected component of a ModelMesh. -1 means none: the component of a
// vertex that no element references.
type MeshComponentIndex
    implements IValue, IHashable, IComparable, IIndex
{
    Value: Integer;
}

// The connected components of a ModelMesh: two elements are in one component when a chain of
// elements, each sharing a vertex with the next, joins them (union-find over element-vertex
// incidence, so two sheets touching at one vertex are one component with a pinched vertex).
// Components are numbered from 0 in the order of their lowest element index. ElementComponent has
// one entry per element, VertexComponent one per vertex, -1 for a vertex no element references.
// ElementParent and ElementDepth are the certificate that each component is connected: a spanning
// forest of the element graph in which each component's lowest element is the root (its own
// parent, depth 0) and every other element's parent shares a vertex with it and is one level
// nearer the root. With them the contract is exact: elements sharing a vertex are in one component
// (Law_ElementCornersShareItsComponent), and elements in one component are joined by a chain (the
// parent chains to the one root), with no reachability form needed in the specification.
type MeshComponents
    implements IValue
{
    ElementComponent: Array<MeshComponentIndex>;
    VertexComponent: Array<MeshComponentIndex>;
    ComponentCount: Integer;
    ElementParent: Array<ElementIndex>;
    ElementDepth: Array<Integer>;
}

// The cell and defect counts of one component. Vertices, Edges (distinct undirected edges),
// Triangles, and Quads are its cells, so its Euler characteristic is
// Vertices - Edges + Triangles + Quads. BoundaryEdges have one element side, NonManifoldEdges more
// than two, MisorientedEdges two sides traversed in the same direction. PinchedVertices are
// vertices whose link is not one cycle or one path: the link of v joins, for each element at v,
// the corner before v to the corner after v. BoundaryCycles is the number of connected pieces of
// the graph of boundary edges; on a surface (no non-manifold edge, no pinched vertex) every
// boundary vertex has exactly two boundary edges, so the pieces are disjoint cycles, the boundary
// circles of the classification chi = 2 - 2g - B. The field names follow 02-topology's ShellCounts.
// The stdlib's TopologySummary is not used: its Manifoldness asserts vertex stars are disks, it has
// no orientation count, and per component its ConnectedComponentCount is always 1.
type MeshComponentCounts
    implements IValue
{
    Vertices: Integer;
    Edges: Integer;
    Triangles: Integer;
    Quads: Integer;
    BoundaryEdges: Integer;
    NonManifoldEdges: Integer;
    MisorientedEdges: Integer;
    PinchedVertices: Integer;
    BoundaryCycles: Integer;
}
